---

This repository ships no compiler binaries. The compiler is copied into `solc-assets/` by `npm start`
and is not in version control; the JavaScript is loaded from a CDN at runtime. All of it is governed by
its own license:

- `solc` (the JavaScript bindings, `solc` on npm): MIT
- The Solidity compiler itself, which is what `soljson.js` is a build of: GPL-3.0
- `@ethereumjs/vm`, `@ethereumjs/util`, `@ethereumjs/common`: MPL-2.0
- `ethers`: MIT

The `solc` npm package declares MIT while wrapping a GPL-3.0 compiler. Anyone redistributing the
compiler, or hosting it as part of a service, should confirm the position for their own case —
see FINDINGS.md §9.
